{"name":"Oatmeal Biscuit","hex":"#b7a86d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oatmeal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Meal made from rolled or round oats.","A breakfast cereal made from rolled oats, cooked in milk or water."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light greyish brown colour, like that of oatmeal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oatmeal"},{"term":"biscuit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, flat, baked good which is either hard and crisp or else soft but firm; a cookie.","A small, usually soft and flaky bread, generally made with baking soda, which is similar in texture to a scone but which is usually not sweet."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fire (pottery) in a kiln, without a ceramic glaze.","To take part in the sport of tubing, riding down a river on an inner tube."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/biscuit"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oatmeal","blocks":[{"text":"Oatmeal is a preparation of oats that have been dehusked, steamed, and flattened, or a coarse flour of hulled oat grains (groats) that have either been milled (ground), rolled, or steel-cut. Ground oats are also called white oats. Steel-cut oats are known as coarse oatmeal, Irish oatmeal, or pinhead oats. Rolled oats were traditionally thick old-fashioned oats, but they can be made thinner or smaller and may be categorized as quick oatmeal or instant oatmeal depending on the cooking time required, which is determined by the size of the oats and the amount of precooking."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Oatmeal.jpg/330px-Oatmeal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oatmeal","wikidata":"Q26883501"},{"title":"Biscuit","blocks":[{"text":"A biscuit is a flour-based baked food item. Biscuits are typically hard, flat, and unleavened. They are usually sweet and may be made with sugar, chocolate, 